 "result_text": "I fixed this in `get_keys` in `sshtunnel.py`. When `host_pkey_directories` is `None` or empty, it now searches the default `~/.ssh` directory (`~/ssh` on Windows) for `id_rsa`, `id_dsa`, `id_ecdsa` and `id_ed25519`. I didn't run any tests, and I didn't add any.\n\nThe `if host_pkey_directories is not None:` guard skipped the whole loop for `None`, so the `or [DEFAULT_SSH_DIRECTORY]` fallback never ran. I removed that guard and de-indented the loop body to match. The rest of the logic is unchanged.\n\nOne behaviour change: `SSHTunnelForwarder` passes `host_pkey_directories=None` by default, so it will now load keys from the default directory in cases where it previously loaded none.",
